From bb0a5bbd35fe147ba18adc242317c5a0a2345d0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:25:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban walls): read the live OAuth pool under
 the home's secret scope in a multiplexing dispatcher, and warn when a pool
 read fails

The mini BB gateway multiplexes profiles, and its dispatcher tick runs in an empty Context with no
secret scope. There get_secret fails closed, so load_pool('anthropic') raised UnscopedSecretError
(the singleton seeder reads ANTHROPIC_TOKEN) on every tick. live_pool_serving swallowed it at DEBUG
and answered False: a disproved hinted anthropic episode kept holding t_01a1cf8766b9af6a and
prune_disproved_walls kept a false anthropic wall, while live_quota_wall failed open. A fresh
process (not multiplexing) read True.

live_quota_wall / live_quota_room / live_pool_serving now bind the home's own secret scope
(owner_secret_scope, as the decomposer tick does) when multiplexing with no scope bound, and judge
the pool inside it; a routed turn's own scope is left alone. A pool read that still fails logs a
WARNING with the provider and exception type, at most once per provider per 15 minutes.
